==Requirement Strategies==
*For the first requirement, focus on picking up [[Research Capsules]] and extracting [[Machines]]. The Machine and Capsule count increases the further you descend, so you can earn more {{II|Ichor|name=true}}.
*For the second requirement, play as {{CI|Scraps|name=true}} and try to complete 3 of her [[Mastery]] Quests by going on multiple runs. Since you only need to complete half of the total mastery quests to buy Goob, choose some specific missions, preferably the easiest ones.

==Strategies==
Goob is a supporter [[Toon]] with excellent mobility and survivability, having 4{{Star}}[[Movement Speed]] and [[Stamina]], which allows Goob to be able to out-walk most of the {{Type|Common}}, {{Type|Uncommon}}, {{Type|Rare}}, and even {{Type|Main}} [[Twisteds]] with the use of speed [[Trinkets]], excluding {{CI|Twisted Pebble|name=true}}, {{CI|Twisted Bobette|name=true}}, {{CI|Twisted Gourdy|name=true}}, {{CI|Twisted Glisten|name=true}} (enraged), and {{CI|Twisted Dyle|name=true}}. Goob also has 2 Star [[Stealth]], which is the same as some Toons such yet as low as many others, making him a great candidate for one of the best distractors in the game.

Goob's main bonus is his Active [[Ability]], {{AI|Goob|name=true}}. This Ability allows him to bring another [[Toon]] towards himself as long as they are in his line of sight. This can be useful in many ways, from saving lives to helping other Toons get around:
*Pulling a Toon away from a Twisted;
*Pulling a Toon into the [[Elevator]] during [[Panic Mode]], including AFK players;
*Pulling a Toon away from a distractor if they're too close or passing Twisteds;
*Pulling a low Movement Speed Toon to help them travel faster;
*Pulling a high Extraction Speed Toon over to a [[Machine]] or Duo Machine to work with them;
*Pulling a Toon away from {{CI|Twisted Razzle & Dazzle|name=true}}'s circle, {{CI|Twisted Rodger|name=true}}'s range when opened, {{CI|Twisted Blot|name=true}}'s hands, and such others;
*Pulling a Toon before they get hit/grabbed by {{CI|Twisted Scraps|name=true}} or {{CI|Twisted Goob|name=true}};
*Pulling Healers/low Health Toons to healing Items;
*Pulling Toons away from Twisted Dyle if being chased by him or if he's nearby.

'''Hug!''' is a generally useful tool for helping out teammates when used correctly. Goob can take advantage of his high Movement Speed and Stamina to get into good places to use his Ability, and with its broad usage, he can make use of it often enough to be worth it. In situations where a Twisted is between you and your hug target, you can use your Ability to pull them directly through the Twisted to safety, as Goob's target is invincible during the pull. Do note that it can be difficult to aim properly, and his pull cancels if line of sight is blocked by an obstacle, so keep in mind that even though there may be no targets on the screen, Goob's Ability may still activate on a nearby Toon if they are in line of sight, making it slightly dangerous if you are being chased/distracting.

As for [[Items]], Goob doesn't need many Speed Items due to his already great mobility, but it could be useful to take Stamina-Restoring Items, such as a {{II|Bottle o' Pop|name=false}}, {{II|Pop|name=false}}, {{II|Stamina Candy|name=false}}, or {{II|Protein Bar|name=false}}. Health items are also great for Goob, as being a Distractor means he is at frequent risk of getting hit. Stamina should be preserved for Panic Mode whenever possible. {{II|Valve|name=false}} and {{II|Jumper Cable|name=false}} are also useful situationally, to help your team with Machines, best used at the start of the floor (if distracting).

Despite Goob's main usage as a distractor, his average Skill Check can make him a possible Extractor if he needs to be, such as if a different player requests to be in the role of distraction or if you're not proficient with it. He's still a proficient supporter if his Ability is used effectively, and can additionally take care of Treadmill Machines with ease. Prioritizing Barnaby Machines can also be efficient since the coins ("Great Job!" Skill Checks) can appear frequently enough to make up for Goob's lower Extraction Speed, especially if you start and stop consistently to get a coin in the first pair of seaweed.

Overall Goob is a great supporter, with a good capability of distracting and survival. He is rather capable at extracting with the right Trinkets and strategy, being a good Toon to have on a team.

