==Trivia==
*Goob used to be one of 4 characters which were original characters before being added to [[Dandy's World]].
**The exact type of OC Goob was based on is currently unknown.
**His name was originally E.G.G., (Especially Good Guy), his feet looked similar to roller skates, he had a tank possibly filled with ichor behind his back, and he even had a feminine human design.<ref>[[File:E.G.G (Old Goob's Design).jpg|200px]]</ref>
*Goob is the younger brother of {{CI|Scraps|name=true}}.
**Despite that, he was created first, with him being SC-014 and Scraps being SC-015.
*Goob's name may be derived from the word "goober," meaning a foolish person. His carefree personality, cross-eyed expression, and slightly clumsy walk are some attributes that can earn him this name, but his understanding and thoughtfulness drive him away from being foolish.
*Goob used to be able to intentionally pull [[Toons]] from the [[Elevator]] into dangerous situations with his [[Ability]], causing them to either take damage or die. If a Goob was caught doing this intentionally, they would likely receive a ban due to the rule of '''No Foul Play/Griefing''' (though if you did so accidentally, it wouldn't be a bannable offense). This is no longer possible in [[Changelog|v0.3]] and beyond.
*{{CI|Shelly|name=true}} and {{CI|Toodles|name=true}} point out that Goob has sharp teeth, being much more obvious when he is hurt and in the mouth of his {{CI|Twisted Goob}}[[Twisted Goob|Twisted counterpart]].
**He, {{CI|Yatta|name=true}}, and {{CI|Eclipse|name=true}} all have sharp teeth, but his are hidden.
*Goob's arms do not highlight when hovered over with an [[Ability]], likely because of how Goob's hands are technically not a part of his model.
**This also happens for [[Scraps]] and her {{CI|Twisted Scraps}}[[Twisted Scraps|Twisted counterpart]].
*Goob's 'fingers' are actually claws. This is confirmed in one of his dialogues after he finishes a [[Machine]].
**This makes Goob (and [[Scraps]]) the first [[Toon]] with claws, with the second being {{CI|Gourdy|name=true}}.
*In [[Roleplay Mode]], Goob and [[Scraps]] share the same room due to their familial relationship.
**It could be implied that them and {{CI|Razzle & Dazzle|name=true}} are the only related [[Toons]] to share the same room, since all the other related duos have an [[Event Toon]] relative whom they don't get to see when it isn't time.
*Goob has an unique extraction animation where he flops his hands onto the valve and down repeatedly.
*When using his [[Ability]], Goob can say "{{Text|Come here!}}" or "{{Text|Get over here! Hehe!}}", referencing Scorpion from Mortal Kombat; he shouts those quotes when using his iconic grapple pull attack.
*Goob, {{CI|Gigi|name=true}}, {{CI|Ginger|name=true}}, [[Pebble]], and {{CI|Tisha|name=true}} all have [[Abilities]] that end with an exclamation mark.
*Unlike [[Scraps]], Goob is not based on any animal in specific. However, due to the shape of bits of fluff on the sides of his head, many believe this to lead to a dog-like design as opposed to Scraps having a feline one. He does have some animal traits, such as being fluffy, shedding (mentioned in his interaction with [[Tisha]]), dreaming about chasing his tail—a behavior typically associated with dogs, even though he doesn't actually have one (mentioned in his interaction with {{CI|Astro|name=true}}), as well as having sharp teeth, claws, and paw-like hands.
**Goob is most likely based on a monster, due to his crossed eyes ([https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strabismus strabismus]) which resemble googly eyes. something that is frequently seen in monster-based crafts, but this depiction is a rarity in the community.
***Due to this, he could be inspired by the term "tickle monster," with the hugs he gives out being somewhat akin to tickling, especially since his hugs are received in mixed ways and are occasionally spontaneous, however this may just be a coincidence.
*{{CI|Poppy|name=true}} and Goob seem to be good friends, as they engage in a friendly shouting match in their interaction. [[Yatta]] also appears to get along with him, as they also yell each other's names when they see each other.
*Goob may have wobbly hands as implied with his interaction with [[Teagan]] in which he mentions that he dropped the teacup last time. This is further implied by his animation whenever he extracts a [[Machine]] as he has to lift his hands constantly, and his dialogue in the [[Art Gallery|Art Floor]] (where he mentions he spilled paint there a while ago). It's unknown if this is due to the material of his arms, or a deficit in motor skills.
*Goob is one of four [[Toons]] that has a fan-made [[Skin]], his being Special Spaghetti. The other three are Dapperly Festive {{CI|Looey|name=true}}, Ebony Detective [[Rodger]], and Choco Cones [[Yatta]].
**Goob's Special Spaghetti skin used to have a glitch with the texture files. The fluff on top of his head matched the same color as his base skin, not the pasta sauce. This was eventually fixed.
*According to [[Dandy]]'s [[gossip]] about Goob, he used to give more hugs than he does now, or rather, he just doesn't hug Dandy as much anymore.
*Goob is the first [[Toon]] to require only half (3 quests) of [[Scraps|another Toon]]'s [[Mastery]], with the second being {{CI|Waxwell|name=true}}. 
**This could reflect how Scraps also needs only half of Goob's [[Twisted Goob|Twisted counterpart]]'s [[Research]].
*Goob is the first [[Toon]] to need another Toon for his Active [[Ability]] to be used.
**[[Scraps]] was on this list, until her Ability was reworked in [[Changelog|v0.7.1]], when she could grapple onto [[Machines]] now.
*Goob, [[Scraps]], and {{CI|Brightney|name=true}} were the last [[Toons]] to get optimized. He is also the last male Toon to receive this treatment.
*Goob is the only [[Toon]] to blink one eye at a time, which can also be referred to as "frog blinking."
**That also makes him the first Toon to have 2 extra blink textures due to this.
***Goob's Special Spaghetti skin is the only Goob skin to not have a right eye blink texture. Instead, he reuses the left eye blink texture twice when blinking. This is very likely a bug.
*After Goob's optimization, his {{Skin|Special Spaghetti}} [[Skin]]'s arms were made thinner in order to resemble spaghetti more.
*When Goob uses his {{AI|Goob|name=true}} Ability with the {{Skin|Special Spaghetti}} or {{Skin|Neapolitan}} [[Skins]] equipped, his arms will become black instead of the actual skin color.
*Prior to his optimization, his arms used the default Roblox Studio rope.
*He is the second non-[[Main Character|Main]] Toon to have an official deluxe plush version of himself.
*Goob may have been the one to create the {{TI|Cardboard 'Armor'|name=true}} [[Trinket]], with him mentioning creating armor out of cardboard in his interaction with {{CI|Soulvester|name=true}} and it needing 100% [[Research]] on his [[Twisted Goob|Twisted counterpart]].
*Goob seems inconsistent with his arms. Sometimes, he can use them normally like hugging or his idle animation, but other times, he moves them flimsily, like his extracting and other animations. This inability to use them properly could just be from his derpy personality and from laziness.
**In fact, Goob seems to be very physically strong, being able to pull all of the [[Toons]] (of which are various sizes and weights) towards himself with ease ([[Looey]] & {{CI|Ribecca|name=true}} even complain about being squeezed too tightly, though this could be because of their fragile bodies).

